From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 15 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Build as C++14 for glog 0.7

wrynose ships glog 0.7.1, where <glog/logging.h> uses std::exchange and
std::make_unique. Both are C++14, and this project pins itself to C++11, so
every translation unit that logs fails to compile:

    glog/logging.h:1262:21: error: 'exchange' is not a member of 'std'
    glog/logging.h:1468:38: error: 'make_unique' is not a member of 'std'

scarthgap had glog 0.6.0, whose headers were still C++11-clean, which is why
this only appears now.

Ask for C++14 rather than the compiler default: it is the minimum glog needs,
and it keeps this Android-derived code away from the C++17 removals.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
 include(FindPkgConfig)
 include(GNUInstallDirs)
 
-set(CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS "${CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS} -std=c++11")
+set(CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS "${CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS} -std=c++14")
 
 add_definitions(-DMTP_DEVICE -DMTP_HOST -D_FILE_OFFSET_BITS=64)
 
